Proposed patch 1 of 2 - NOT APPLIED.

    file:   /opt/etravel-ai-ops/app/main.py
    adds:   GET /node/v1/sites
    why:    Nothing on the controller returns the 126-site inventory. /health
            gives counts only and /fleet/status returns the four node statuses,
            so ai1 has no way to answer "list every eShops site" no matter how
            it authenticates. This adds one read-only route beside the two
            /node/v1/ routes that already exist, using the same HMAC check, and
            reads the same /etc/etravel-ai-ops/sites.yml - it does not create a
            second inventory.

    safety: read-only; no write path; already-existing auth; /node/v1/ is
            exempt from the browser session middleware by design
            (app/local_auth.py route_is_public), so no new public surface.

